## Summary

I delivered a production-quality native Apple (SwiftUI + Swift Charts) parity of `BatteryRangeCharts`, committed as `9a412ff6a`.

**What shipped** (13 files in `apps/apple/TeslaSync/feature-views/BatteryRangeCharts.*`, decomposed per the established sibling architecture):
- **Battery Overview panel**: radial gauge + Battery/Range readouts + Current-vs-Remaining `BarMark` chart (web `CHART_COLORS[0]`, 0–100 axis).
- **Drive Distance Trend panel**: distance + duration `AreaMark`/`LineMark` series (`CHART_COLORS[0]`/`[1]`) with legend, tooltips and an `AXChartDescriptor`, or the "No drive data for chart" empty state.
- **All states**: loading skeleton, empty (`ContentUnavailableView`), error+retry (`QueryError` peer), stale (chip + one-shot auto-refresh), offline (cached chip) — plus the web per-panel empty branch.
- Binds through the shared **P1/S8** `BatteryRangeChartsSource` (no HTTP in the view); every string via the **P1/S10** facade; VoiceOver labels everywhere; **P1/S11** `view.opened`; SI-only math at the render boundary; adapter/projection/math/a11y/model unit tests + per-state previews.

**Verification (all green):** `swiftformat --lint` 0/12 · `swiftlint --strict` 0 violations · placeholder scan COUNT=0 · full `swiftc -typecheck` of every shipped + test file against the **real** design tokens and Charts/Accessibility frameworks (exit 0) · xcodegen integrates the files into the app + test targets · KMP `Shared.xcframework` built & staged.

